WEBVTT

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:06.740
Question 5 would let Rhode Island borrow $55 million for environmental and recreational purposes.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:12.130
A bond is a loan, repaid with interest from the state's general revenues.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:17.510
Each of five bond questions is decided separately, by majority vote.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:22.640
A fund for local infrastructure resilience gets $25 million.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.530
$12 million would improve State parks, beaches and campgrounds.

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:33.310
Six others, from brownfield cleanup to open space, get smaller amounts.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:45.790
The handbook estimates $33,267,500 in interest, a total cost of $88,267,500.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:51.080
Those are only estimates, based on 20-year loans at 5 percent interest.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:55.310
The handbook includes no official argument against the question.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:59.670
The handbook includes no official argument for the question.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:04.150
Approve means you support the State issuing these bonds.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:08.400
Reject means you are against the State issuing these bonds.
